  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10a-2010-p5.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Recall that the formula for the circumference of a circle is \\(2 \\pi r.\\) We then have that \\[ 24\\pi = 2\\pi r \\]\\[ r = 12. \\]\n\nThe area of a circle is \\(\\pi r^2,\\) so we have that \\[ k \\pi = \\pi 12^2 \\]\\[ k = 144. \\]\n\nThus, E is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "Use the circumference to find the radius first",
        "From \\(2\\pi r=24\\pi\\), the desired \\(k\\) is \\(r^2\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
